<decisions #define-ai-workflow-foundation-on-depa-flows {
  version = "1"
}
(
  <decision #track.foundation.package_shape {
    status = "accepted"
    priority = "P0"
  }
  (
    <question ?>Where should shared AI workflow contracts live?</?>
    <answer ?>Create a small shared foundation contract package and a matching logic package.</?>
    <rationale ?>This avoids coupling the two profile implementations while keeping shared runtime vocabulary consistent.</?>
  )>

  <decision #track.foundation.substrate_binding {
    status = "accepted"
    priority = "P0"
  }
  (
    <question ?>How should substrate ownership be encoded?</?>
    <answer ?>Export descriptors that explicitly bind AI Ctrl Workflow to WorkCtrlFlow and AI Data Workflow to EagerDataFlow.</?>
    <rationale ?>A typed descriptor makes the no-alternate-engine constraint visible to downstream code.</?>
  )>

  <decision #track.foundation.effect_boundary {
    status = "accepted"
    priority = "P0"
  }
  (
    <question ?>How are AI effects and runtime roots supplied?</?>
    <answer ?>They are runtime/config inputs supplied by the wrapper; foundation logic does not construct host-specific implementations.</?>
    <rationale ?>This preserves the DEPA effect boundary and keeps core helpers testable.</?>
  )>
)>
